Subject: a first-use load short of memory for its first records says so

The two records a load allocates first (the module and its file) went
short with the root-pass line whatever the load was; outside the root
pass they now print the first-use line of patch 0049.

--- a/dlm_core.c
+++ b/dlm_core.c
@@ -928,7 +928,11 @@
 			dlm_free((char *)m, (long)sizeof (struct dlm_mod));
 		if (lf)
 			dlm_free((char *)lf, (long)sizeof (struct dlm_lf));
-		printf("dlm: %s: no memory for it in the root pass\n", name);
+		if (dlm_nosleep)
+			printf("dlm: %s: no memory for it in the root pass\n", name);
+		else
+			printf("dlm: %s: not loaded: kernel memory short (error %d)\n",
+			    name, ENOMEM);
 		return ENOMEM;
 	}
 	strcpy(m->m_name, name);
